        "original_id": "5dc09146-0083-5ba3-939a-546eca133db7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bagsecg, King Ethelred, Alfred the Great\n- Events: Battle of Ashdown\n- Places: Berkshire, Oxfordshire\n- Roles: Viking leader, king, West Saxon Army leaders\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Ashdown took place on 8 January 871 in Berkshire, possibly in the part that is now in Oxfordshire.\n- Bagsecg, also known as Bægsecg or Bagsec, was a Viking leader commonly referred to as a king.\n- Bagsecg was killed on 8 January 871 at the Battle of Ashdown.\n- The West Saxon Army at the Battle of Ashdown was led by King Ethelred and his younger brother, the future Alfred the Great.",
